{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
  "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case involves the -- the constitutionality of two congressional districts in North Carolina that should be familiar to the Court because they've been before the Court on multiple prior occasions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument in Case 15-1262, McCrory v. Harris."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Clement, that passage in -- in Cromartie II says in a case like this one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: If they really just wanted to help the Democrats hurt the Republicans or vice versa --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: To what extent and what circumstances does Section 5 of the Voting Rights Act require that a contiguous district be drawn in order to comply with strict scrutiny? Assume that you're using race and then you have to comply with strict scrutiny."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Did they -- did they in respect to this district, District 12? Because when I go back to Cromartie II, I think he's right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Did the State ever put on any evidence that that was necessary to avoid a retrogression problem under Section 5?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Trial Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The trial court also discounted the testimony that you -- that -- that my -- my good friend and colleague has -- has suggested was offered by the map drawer, Mr. Hofeller, about what he was told and that he only used -- that he turned off race and he only used partisanship. That whole -- that whole analysis, the district court didn't credit. Didn't credit. Said that I -- I heard the testimony. I did what a trier of fact did. I listened to the live witnesses, and I didn't credit it. It wasn't believable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: There was another case -- it was in the State court -- the same issues; just decided the opposite way. We're hearing this case, and you are urging that the plain error to your error is the -- is the legal standard by which we should judge what the three-judge court did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Elias",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELIAS: Your Honor, I think two responses. First is, the -- the Court applies clear error to the case before it where there's a finding of fact by the trier of fact. And that's the -- that's the rules of -- of appellate procedure. That's what this Court has done for many, many years, and it is what my clients are entitled to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would point you to Appendix B, 161 through 163, which are the relevant fact findings of the State trial court, where they were unanimous in finding, among other things, quote, \"Dr. Hofeller constructed the 2011 12th Congressional District based on whole voter tabulation districts in which President Obama received the highest voter totals during the 2008 election.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One reason they didn't do it is because in all of these cases, they thought that as long as they could get the State to say, we had a BVAP floor of 50.1, or 55 point -- percent, we've off the strict scrutiny land, so we don't need a map on predominance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The second reason is, most of these challenges are brought by people who are at least as concerned about Democratic political prospects as they are about avoiding race."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1262",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "05f4867845496e3eb10bce3ec0b061391099cc0aa18ae93aeec656107907419d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f486784549-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You didn't respond to it."
    },
    {
